# The rows of src/runtime/recipes/vulpen/library/parts/modes/Modes.cpp, a call each (src/tools/bench/bench.py).

## Modes.cpp/Modes::begins_to_perform
1 p1 hosted and presented at the first frame -> sent ["gpu"]; edit (10,20)+(200,100), perform (0,0)+(0,0); pointer held 1
2 p2, which draws nothing, hosted -> sent ["ide: param set ide.preview shown first"]; edit (10,20)+(200,100), perform (0,0)+(0,0); pointer held 1
3 p2 presented -> sent ["ide: param set ide.preview shown first"]; edit (10,20)+(200,100), perform (0,0)+(0,0); pointer held 1
4 p2 draws at last -> sent ["ide: panel show ide.perform"]; edit (10,20)+(200,100), perform (0,0)+(0,0); pointer held 1
5 p3, which draws, hosted -> sent ["ide: param set ide.preview shown first"]; edit (10,20)+(200,100), perform (0,0)+(0,0); pointer held 1
6 the same again -> sent []; edit (10,20)+(200,100), perform (0,0)+(0,0); pointer held 1
6b p4, which draws, hosted and switched to, as view load does -> sent ["ide: param set ide.preview shown first", "ide: panel show ide.perform"]; edit (10,20)+(200,100), perform (0,0)+(0,0); pointer held 1
7 p3 presented, the switch on its first half -> sent []; edit (10,20)+(200,100), perform (0,0)+(0,0); pointer held 1
8 p1 presented, the switch's shown unset -> sent []; edit (10,20)+(200,100), perform (0,0)+(0,0); pointer held 1
no shows nor switch, p1 hosted later -> sent []; edit (10,20)+(200,100), perform (0,0)+(0,0); pointer held 1
the device goes -> done

## Modes.cpp/Modes::bind
[("mode", "edit"), ("shows", "ide.perform"), ("switch", "ide.preview")] -> asked ["input area", "input typed", "output edit", "output perform", "output buttons", "command mode edit: gives the window to the dock, which shows what is presented in its panel", "command mode perform: gives the window to what is presented, and the dock no room", "command mode toggle: switches to the other mode"]; buttons edit > mode edit, lit, toggles; run > mode perform, toggles; |; gpu > gpu toggle, lit, toggles, stuck
[("mode", "edit")] -> asked ["input area", "input typed", "output edit", "output perform", "output buttons", "command mode edit: gives the window to the dock, which shows what is presented in its panel", "command mode perform: gives the window to what is presented, and the dock no room", "command mode toggle: switches to the other mode"]; buttons edit > mode edit, lit, toggles; run > mode perform, toggles; |; gpu > gpu toggle, lit, toggles, stuck
[("mode", "perform"), ("shows", "ide.perform"), ("switch", "ide.preview")] -> asked ["input area", "input typed", "output edit", "output perform", "output buttons", "command mode edit: gives the window to the dock, which shows what is presented in its panel", "command mode perform: gives the window to what is presented, and the dock no room", "command mode toggle: switches to the other mode"]; buttons edit > mode edit, toggles; run > mode perform, lit, toggles; |; gpu > gpu toggle, lit, toggles, stuck
[("mode", "run"), ("shows", "ide.perform"), ("switch", "ide.preview")] -> throws runtime_error: "param mode = run: edit or perform"
the device goes -> done

## Modes.cpp/Modes::cook
a warning logged -> sent ["gpu"]; edit (0,0)+(0,0), perform (10,20)+(200,100); pointer ["p1 at (43.33333 20) size (133.33334 100)"]
an error logged -> sent ["mode edit"]; edit (0,0)+(0,0), perform (10,20)+(200,100); pointer ["p1 at (43.33333 20) size (133.33334 100)"]
edit, another key -> sent []; edit (10,20)+(200,100), perform (0,0)+(0,0); pointer held 1
edit, escape -> sent ["gpu", "type quit"]; edit (10,20)+(200,100), perform (0,0)+(0,0); pointer held 1
edit, escape let go -> sent []; edit (10,20)+(200,100), perform (0,0)+(0,0); pointer held 1
edit, escape to the editor in focus -> sent []; edit (10,20)+(200,100), perform (0,0)+(0,0); pointer held 1
escape, p1 presented -> sent []; edit (0,0)+(0,0), perform (10,20)+(200,100); pointer ["p1 at (43.33333 20) size (133.33334 100)"]
nothing presented, none hosted -> sent ["mode edit"]; edit (0,0)+(0,0), perform (10,20)+(200,100); pointer none
p1 presented, no longer hosted -> sent []; edit (0,0)+(0,0), perform (10,20)+(200,100); pointer ["p1 at (43.33333 20) size (133.33334 100)"]
perform, p1 presented -> sent ["gpu"]; edit (0,0)+(0,0), perform (10,20)+(200,100); pointer ["p1 at (43.33333 20) size (133.33334 100)"]
the device goes -> done

## Modes.cpp/Modes::cook, its view edited in the frame
1 the first frame -> sent ["gpu"]; pointer []
2 p1 hosted, the view edited before -> sent [": param set ide.preview shown first"]; pointer []
3 p2 hosted, drawing and presented, the view edited before -> sent [": param set ide.preview shown first", ": panel show ide.perform"]; pointer []
4 in perform mode, the view edited before -> sent []; pointer ["p2 at (43.33333 20) size (133.33334 100)"]
5 an error logged, the view edited before -> sent ["mode edit"]; pointer ["p2 at (43.33333 20) size (133.33334 100)"]
the device goes -> done

## Modes.cpp/Modes::hold
edit, p1 presented -> sent ["gpu"]; edit (10,20)+(200,100), perform (0,0)+(0,0); pointer held 1
no window size -> sent []; edit (0,0)+(0,0), perform (10,20)+(200,100); pointer ["p1 at (10 20) size (0 0)"]
p1 hosted, none presented -> sent []; edit (0,0)+(0,0), perform (10,20)+(200,100); pointer none
perform, p1 presented, the window 400x300 -> sent ["gpu"]; edit (0,0)+(0,0), perform (10,20)+(200,100); pointer ["p1 at (43.33333 20) size (133.33334 100)"]
the device goes -> done
the window 100x400 -> sent []; edit (0,0)+(0,0), perform (10,20)+(200,100); pointer ["p1 at (97.5 20) size (25 100)"]

## Modes.cpp/Modes::switch_mode
edit -> sent ["ide: focus ide.editor", "ide: param set ide.modes mode edit"]; answered ["went to edit mode: the window shows the dock"]
edit again, in edit mode -> sent ["ide: param set ide.modes mode edit"]; answered ["went to edit mode: the window shows the dock"]
perform again, in perform mode -> sent ["ide: param set ide.modes mode perform"]; answered ["went to perform mode: the window shows what is presented"]
perform, nothing hosted -> sent []; answered ["stayed in edit mode, as nothing is presented to perform; view load <project> or view switch <name> presents one"]
perform, p1 hosted, none presented yet -> sent ["ide: focus", "ide: param set ide.modes mode perform"]; answered ["went to perform mode: the window shows what is presented"]
perform, p1 presented, the editor in focus -> sent ["ide: focus", "ide: param set ide.modes mode perform"]; answered ["went to perform mode: the window shows what is presented"]
the device goes -> done
toggle in perform mode, nothing hosted -> sent ["ide: param set ide.modes mode edit"]; answered ["went to edit mode: the window shows the dock"]
toggle, in edit mode -> sent ["ide: focus", "ide: param set ide.modes mode perform"]; answered ["went to perform mode: the window shows what is presented"]
toggle, in perform mode -> sent ["ide: param set ide.modes mode edit"]; answered ["went to edit mode: the window shows the dock"]

## Modes.cpp/Modes::watch_buttons
1 nothing hosted -> sent ["gpu"]; buttons edit > mode edit, lit, toggles; run > mode perform, toggles, stuck; |; gpu > gpu toggle, lit, toggles, stuck
2 again -> sent []; buttons edit > mode edit, lit, toggles; run > mode perform, toggles, stuck; |; gpu > gpu toggle, lit, toggles, stuck
3 the answer now discrete, unasked -> sent []; buttons edit > mode edit, lit, toggles; run > mode perform, toggles, stuck; |; gpu > gpu toggle, lit, toggles, stuck
4 a warning logged -> sent ["gpu"]; buttons edit > mode edit, lit, toggles; run > mode perform, toggles, stuck; |; gpu > gpu toggle, lit, toggles, number, stuck
5 p1 hosted -> sent ["ide: param set ide.preview shown first"]; buttons edit > mode edit, lit, toggles; run > mode perform, toggles; |; gpu > gpu toggle, lit, toggles, number, stuck
6 a window open -> sent []; buttons edit > mode edit, lit, toggles; run > mode perform, toggles; |; gpu > gpu toggle, lit, toggles, number, stuck; fps, muted
7 a warning, the answer naming none -> sent ["gpu"]; buttons edit > mode edit, lit, toggles; run > mode perform, toggles; |; gpu > gpu toggle, lit, toggles, stuck; fps, muted
the device goes -> done
